<title>AUSTRALIA: Cortecs granted U.S. patent for flu vaccine.</title>
<headline>Cortecs granted U.S. patent for flu vaccine.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Drug developer Cortecs International Ltd said on Monday it had been granted a U.S. patent for its Flustat oral influenza vaccine.</p>
<p>On June 30 the company said Flustat trails were on the right track after safely introducing the vaccine into normal humans.</p>
<p>Cortecs said the vaccine was indevelopment at the Australian Institute of Mucosal Immunology in Newcastle in New South Wales.</p>
<p>The company said results from early low dose section of the escalating dose study had shown encouraging local and systemic immune responses at low doses of the vaccine.</p>
</text>
